    "title": "Dana Point Market, June 2026: Six Months of Inventory Down to Ten Weeks | Adam Boehrer, Pacific Sotheby's",
    "headline": "Six months to ten weeks: the Dana Point shift.",
    "lede": "A year ago Dana Point was clearing its inventory in about six months. This spring it is closer to ten weeks, and homes under $5M are closing at list in under two weeks. That is the steepest one-year shift of any town in the South OC coastal peer set.",
    "description": "Dana Point single-family homes sold in a median 12 days in April 2026, less than half of last April's 32, with supply down to 3.1 months from 4.8 and a $2.99M median. The harbor rebuild is visibly underway. By Adam Boehrer, Pacific Sotheby's International Realty.",
